mula, we rewrite them as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{x \\ln y}{\\ln x} = 10 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\frac{4y \\ln x}{\\ln y} = 10.\n\\]\n\nFrom the first, \\(\\frac{\\ln y}{\\ln x} = \\frac{10}{x}\\); from the second, \\(\\frac{\\ln x}{\\ln y} = \\frac{10}{4y} = \\frac{5}{2y}\\). Since these two ratios are reciprocals, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{x} = \\frac{1}{\\frac{5}{2y}} = \\frac{2y}{5}.\n\\]\n\nCross-multiplying gives \\(50 = 2xy\\), so \\(xy = 25\\).\n\nThus, the value of \\(xy\\) is \\(\\boxed{25}\\).<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>"] reward={'score': 1.0, 'acc': True, 'pred': '25'}
